domain ADR0048:
  description "Accepted explicit public V3 guidance profile projection"
evidence OWNER_ACCEPTANCE:
  "Owner authorizes manual Grok CLI export conversion and V3 revision registration for every remaining character on 2026-10-03, under ADR0043's permitted manual route."
evidence FAILURE:
  "First migrated cat retains selectorless statements in consciousGuidance, but old V3 profile adaptation drops that collection; stateless CLI review rejects unchanged public profile for missing allowed support facts."
premise BOUNDARY:
  "V3 guidance is distinct from executable norms. Public facts require explicit disclosure authority; schema conformance does not justify fake selectors or unrelated field copies."
decision ACCEPTANCE based_on OWNER_ACCEPTANCE, FAILURE, BOUNDARY:
  "Execute the explicitly authorized manual all-character migration under ADR0043, including this concrete support-projection repair required to preserve meaning and existing public rights. ADR0048 is Accepted; no new import endpoint or relaxed V3 schema is authorized."
decision PROJECTOR based_on ACCEPTANCE, FAILURE, BOUNDARY:
  "Add a shared typed V3 profile source projector. Retain old facts and ordering; append only statement facts explicitly authorized by an unconditional public profile guidance-path rule. Never project guidance description or infer public rights. Candidate readiness uses this projector."
decision MIGRATION based_on PROJECTOR, BOUNDARY:
  "Copy existing unconditional public norm-statement permission only to the exact mapped guidance statement for that source norm. Legacy source without such permission gets none. Preserve authoritative definitions, prior revisions, bound battles and operational facts."
decision VALIDATION based_on PROJECTOR, MIGRATION:
  "Test unchanged old projection without new permissions, public-only statement source, denial of owner conditional and unrelated paths, and true candidate readiness. Deploy verified validator before affected candidate activation; preserve actual CLI assessments and failures."
